## Embedded victory media (residual risk)

The lab's shipped default victory screen is an **original CSS animation**
authored for this project — it requires no third-party asset and ships with
zero Hunter × Hunter image or video files. See `templates/victory.html`.

Separately, the lab supports an **opt-in** asset slot: if the repository's
operator manually drops a file at `static/img/victory/<node-id>.gif`, the
victory screen will layer it in. Any such file is third-party copyrighted
media (a frame or clip from the Hunter × Hunter anime/manga) that the
operator has chosen to add locally. It is:

- not authored by this project,
- not covered by the MIT license above,
- not distributed by this repository (the build/CI pipeline never fetches,
  bundles, or commits these files — see `assets/README.md` and
  `assets/fetch-assets.sh`, both of which leave the actual source URLs for
  the operator to supply),
- and, in plain terms: **a residual legal risk the operator accepts
  personally** by adding it. No license text — from this project or anyone
  else — can retroactively grant rights to someone else's copyrighted
  artwork. The only real protections available are (a) not distributing
  those frames, and (b) this disclaimer. Keeping the default (original
  animation, no gif) avoids the risk entirely.

